 {"id":"fabro-d5fd","title":"Develop planner: probe unfiltered sd list before parking on an empty assignee-filtered view","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.219Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:26:05.721Z","description":"This run's implementer smoke test showed 'sd ready --assignee nonexistentuser' exits 0 with "No ready issues." — byte-identical to a legitimately empty pool — so under the new park semantics a typo'd or renamed assignee silently parks the line forever. Change: in the FAIL-CLOSED paragraph at .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md:46, before routing Tracker empty, run one unfiltered 'sd list --limit 5' probe; if open seeds exist but the filtered view is empty, journal "park: N open seeds, none assigned to fabro" so the terminal Slack notification shows a cause. Effect: converts a silent permanent outage into a visible, diagnosable park; zero added cost in normal runs. Related: fabro-5e09 (the assignee filter this builds on).
